    "termsOfAccess": "Data usage statement: \n\nDear user, \n\nYou are welcome to download the materials of the Dataverse folder entitled “Data package to ‘The role of autonomy-connectedness in stress-buffering effects of social support in women: An experimental study using a virtual Trier Social Stress Test’”, provided you agree with the following conditions: \n\n1. The downloader undertakes to keep confidential any information in the present data concerning individual persons, households, enterprises or institutions which comes to his/her knowledge during the work on the data. \n\n2. They undertake not to distribute data to others without written permission from L. E. Kunst. \n\n3. They undertake to use the present data for purely scientific (i.e. non-commercial) research only. \n\n4. They contact at least one of the (co-)authors, in case they want to publish or report on these dataset(s). If appropriate, they agree to include a member of this research group as co-author. \n\n5. They include the following acknowledgement in any publication based on the present dataset(s): In this paper use is made of data of Riem, M.M.E., Kunst, L.E., Bekker, M.H.J., Fallon, M., Kupper, N. (2020). Intranasal oxytocin enhances stress-protective effects of social support in women with negative childhood experiences during a Virtual Trier Social Stress Test. Psychoneuroendocrinology, 111, 104482.\n\n6. Downloading the materials does not grant exclusivity on the data or the subject. In the situation when proposals with a comparable subject will be submitted, agreement will be sought between the different parties. \n\n7. This statement shall remain valid, even after conclusion of the work of the present data. \n\n\n",
